        -:  155:/*-
        -:  156: * The error code packs differently depending on if it records a system
        -:  157: * error or an OpenSSL error.
        -:  158: *
        -:  159: * A system error packs like this (we follow POSIX and only allow positive
        -:  160: * numbers that fit in an |int|):
        -:  161: *
        -:  162: * +-+-------------------------------------------------------------+
        -:  163: * |1|                     system error number                     |
        -:  164: * +-+-------------------------------------------------------------+
        -:  165: *
        -:  166: * An OpenSSL error packs like this:
        -:  167: *
        -:  168: * <---------------------------- 32 bits -------------------------->
        -:  169: *    <--- 8 bits ---><------------------ 23 bits ----------------->
        -:  170: * +-+---------------+---------------------------------------------+
        -:  171: * |0|    library    |                    reason                   |
        -:  172: * +-+---------------+---------------------------------------------+
        -:  173: *
        -:  174: * A few of the reason bits are reserved as flags with special meaning:
        -:  175: *
        -:  176: *                    <5 bits-<>--------- 19 bits ----------------->
        -:  177: *                   +-------+-+-----------------------------------+
        -:  178: *                   | rflags| |          reason                   |
        -:  179: *                   +-------+-+-----------------------------------+
        -:  180: *                            ^
        -:  181: *                            |
        -:  182: *                           ERR_RFLAG_FATAL = ERR_R_FATAL
        -:  183: *
        -:  184: * The reason flags are part of the overall reason code for practical
        -:  185: * reasons, as they provide an easy way to place different types of
        -:  186: * reason codes in different numeric ranges.
        -:  187: *
        -:  188: * The currently known reason flags are:
        -:  189: *
        -:  190: * ERR_RFLAG_FATAL      Flags that the reason code is considered fatal.
        -:  191: *                      For backward compatibility reasons, this flag
        -:  192: *                      is also the code for ERR_R_FATAL (that reason
        -:  193: *                      code served the dual purpose of flag and reason
        -:  194: *                      code in one in pre-3.0 OpenSSL).
        -:  195: * ERR_RFLAG_COMMON     Flags that the reason code is common to all
        -:  196: *                      libraries.  All ERR_R_ macros must use this flag,
        -:  197: *                      and no other _R_ macro is allowed to use it.
        -:  198: */
        -:  199:
        -:  200:/* Macros to help decode recorded system errors */
        -:  201:#define ERR_SYSTEM_FLAG ((unsigned int)INT_MAX + 1)
